.TH PROXMOX-NAG-REMOVER 8 "September 2026" "proxmox-nag-remover" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
proxmox-nag-remover \- manage the Proxmox VE subscription-dialog patch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proxmox-nag-remover
.RI [ apply | status | restore ]
.RI [ --target\  PATH ]
.RI [ --no-restart ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proxmox-nag-remover
applies, reports, or safely restores a narrowly targeted modification to the
Proxmox VE web interface's no-subscription dialog.
The package's APT hook runs
.B apply
after package transactions so Proxmox widget-toolkit upgrades are patched
again when their layout is supported.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Patch the supported subscription-dialog call. This is the default command.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the target is patched, unpatched, or unsupported.
.TP
.B restore
Restore the saved upstream file only when the current target exactly matches
the patch generated from that backup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --target\  PATH
Operate on an alternate file. This option is primarily intended for testing.
.TP
.B --no-restart
Do not restart
.BR pveproxy (8)
after changing the target.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show a short usage message.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/javascript/proxmox-widget-toolkit/proxmoxlib.js
Default patch target.
.TP
.I /usr/share/javascript/proxmox-widget-toolkit/proxmoxlib.js.proxmox-nag-remover.bak
Saved upstream file used for guarded restoration.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99proxmox-nag-remover
APT hook that reapplies the patch after package operations.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. For
.BR status ,
zero means patched, one means unpatched or missing, and two means the target
layout is unsupported.
